# Modal File Structure

When the project uses `web/components/modals/`, every modal lives in its own folder with exactly two files:

- `index.tsx` — all component logic, state, and JSX (default export)
- `styles.css` — co-located styles, imported inside `index.tsx`

```
// ❌ BAD — separate component file + re-export barrel
web/components/modals/MyModal/
  MyModal.tsx      ← logic
  index.ts         ← export { default } from "./MyModal"
  styles.css

// ✅ GOOD — all logic directly in index.tsx
web/components/modals/MyModal/
  index.tsx        ← logic + JSX, default export
  styles.css
```

Import by folder path (adjust alias to match the project's tsconfig):

```tsx
import MyModal from "@/components/modals/MyModal";
```

Styling follows [ui-primitives-first.mdc](ui-primitives-first.mdc) — tokens from `globals.css`, semantic tags for typography, and all modal-specific styles in that modal's co-located `styles.css`.
